      "text": "To find the perimeter of the triangle, we add up the lengths of all three sides. The lengths of the sides are 14 cm, 8 cm, and 9 cm. So, the perimeter is:\n\nPerimeter = 14 cm + 8 cm + 9 cm = 31 cm\n\nThe final answer is \\boxed{31}.\n\nWhat is the sum of the solutions of the equation $(3x+5)(2x-9) = 0$? Express your answer as a common fraction.\nTo solve the equation \\((3x+5)(2x-9) = 0\\), we need to find the values of \\(x\\) that satisfy the equation by setting each factor equal to zero. This is because a product of factors is zero if and only if at least one of the factors is zero.\n\nFirst, consider the equation \\(3x + 5 = 0\\):\n\\[\n3x + 5 = 0\n\\]\nSubtract 5 from both sides:\n\\[\n3x = -5\n\\]\nDivide both sides by 3:\n\\[\nx = -\\frac{5}{3}\n\\]\n\nNext, consider the equation \\(2x - 9 = 0\\):\n\\[\n2x - 9 = 0\n\\]\nAdd 9 to both sides:\n\\[\n2x = 9\n\\]\nDivide both sides by 2:\n\\[\nx = \\frac{9}{2}\n\\]\n\nThe solutions to the equation \\((3x+5)(2x-9) = 0\\) are \\(x = -\\frac{5}{3}\\) and \\(x = \\frac{9}{2}\\). To find the sum of these solutions, we add them together:\n\\[\n-\\frac{5}{3} + \\frac{9}{2}\n\\]\n\nTo add these fractions, we need a common denominator. The least common multiple of 3 and 2 is 6. We convert each fraction to have this common denominator:\n\\[\n-\\frac{5}{3} = -\\frac{5 \\times 2}{3 \\times 2} = -\\frac{10}{6}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{9}{2} = \\frac{9 \\times 3}{2 \\times 3} = \\frac{27}{6}\n\\]\n\nNow we can add the fractions:\n\\[\n-\\frac{10}{6} + \\frac{27}{6} = \\frac{-10 + 27}{6} = \\frac{17}{6}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the solutions is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{17}{6}}\\).\n\nIn triangle $\\triangle ABC$, the sides opposite to angles $A$, $B$, and $C$ are $a$, $b$, and $c$ respectively. If $b=2$, $c=2\\sqrt{3}$, and $A=30^{\\circ}$, then the area of $\\triangle ABC$ is ______.\nTo find the area of triangle \\(\\triangle ABC\\) with sides \\(b = 2\\), \\(c = 2\\sqrt{3}\\), and angle \\(A = 30^\\circ\\), we can use 